{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-13762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the product ${I}_{2}B$ given that ${I}_{2}$ is the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix and\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-13762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix ${I}_{2}$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\n{I}_{2}\\cdot B=B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-13762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4365440057493f60dc29fe8f63f7736b97744b7a6b03774345cdab7e0f4a7dd7"} {"question" "q-13762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-13762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["text" "The product is undefined"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-13762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-75479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the product $Q{I}_{2}$ given that ${I}_{2}$ is the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix and\n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-75479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $Q$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and ${I}_{2}$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\nQ\\cdot {I}_{2}=Q=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-75479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/activity-metad