anged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix ${I}_{3}$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $K$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\n{I}_{3}\\cdot K=K=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-75474" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4365440057493f60dc29fe8f63f7736b97744b7a6b03774345cdab7e0f4a7dd7"} {"question" "q-75474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-75474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-75474" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the product $Q{I}_{3}$ given that ${I}_{3}$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix and\n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Q\\cdot {I}_{3}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-7}} | {{field-8}} | {{field-9}} |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $Q$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and ${I}_{3}$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\nQ\\cdot {I}_{3}=Q=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337652" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4365440057493f60dc29fe8f63f7736b97744b7a6b03774345cdab7e0f4a7dd7"} {"question" "q-337652" "field" "field-1" "att