ke/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-75472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix ${I}_{2}$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $G$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\n{I}_{2}\\cdot G=G=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-75472" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4365440057493f60dc29fe8f63f7736b97744b7a6b03774345cdab7e0f4a7dd7"} {"question" "q-75472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-75472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-75472" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-130247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-130247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $B$ is the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3},$ the result must be the $2$nd *column* of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot 0+(\\frac{-\\sqrt{2}}{2})\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot 0+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0 \\\\ 0\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-130247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4365440057493f60dc29fe8f63f7736b97744b7a6b03774345cdab7e0f4a7dd7"} {"question" "q-130247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-130247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & 0\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-130247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the product $AB,$ if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & -2\\sqrt{6} \\\\ -1 & 7 & \\sqrt{6} \\\\ 5 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $B$ is the $3$rd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $3$rd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3},$ the result must be the $3$rd *column* of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{6} \\\\ \\sqrt{6} \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & -2\\sqrt{6} \\\\ -1 & 7 & \\sqrt{6} \\\\ 5 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot 0+(-2\\sqrt{6})\\cdot 1 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot 0+7\\cdot 0+\\sqrt{6}\\cdot 1 \\\\ 5\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 0+(-8)\\cdot 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{6} \\\\ \\sqrt{6} \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4365440057493f60dc29fe8f63f7736b97744b7a6b03774345cdab7e0f4a7dd7"} {"question" "q-337661" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337661" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2\\sqrt{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337661" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337661" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337661" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337661" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-8"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337673" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the product $EF$, if\n$E=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$F=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & -8 & \\sqrt{5} & 14 \\\\ -2 & \\frac{7}{5} & -\\frac{\\pi }{2} & 9 \\\\ \\sqrt{17} & -6 & 0 & \\frac{e}{3} \\\\ -11 & \\sqrt{19} & -4 & -\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)\\end{aligned}].$\n\n| $EF=$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337673" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $E$ is the $4$th *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{4}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $4\\times 4$ matrix $F$ by the $4$th *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{4}$ on the *left*, the result must be the $4$th *row* of $F.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nEF=[\\begin{aligned}-11 & \\sqrt{19} & -4 & -\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}EF & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & -8 & \\sqrt{5} & 14 \\\\ -2 & \\frac{7}{5} & -\\frac{\\pi }{2} & 9 \\\\ \\sqrt{17} & -6 & 0 & \\frac{e}{3} \\\\ -11 & \\sqrt{19} & -4 & -\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 & \\sqrt{19} & -4 & -\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337673" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4365440057493f60dc29fe8f63f7736b97744b7a6b03774345cdab7e0f4a7dd7"} {"question" "q-337673" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337673" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-11"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337673" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337673" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{19}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337673" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337673" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337673" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-337673" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\ln(3)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-41949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{7} & -3 & 3.5 \\\\ -2 & 2\\sqrt{5} & -2.5 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978659/state.json" "file_sha256" "eca123e1f23257b5e527d038cb945846f6f4d5b321191a191755ec365d6cf2e3"} {"question" "q-41949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $B$ is the $1$st *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $1$st *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3},$ the result must be the $1$st *column* of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{7} \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{7} & -3 & 3.5 \\\\ -2 & 2\\sqrt{5} & -2.5 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{7}\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 0+3.5\\cdot 0 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 1+2\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 0+(-2.5)\\cdot 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 0+5\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{7} \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/C